Meridian Electronics — AI Customer Support Platform

This repository contains a production-ready AI-powered customer support system for Meridian Electronics. The platform enables users to check product availability, manage orders, and handle account inquiries through a secure, tool-augmented conversational agent.

Beyond a simple chatbot, this system demonstrates robust AI orchestration, safety guardrails, infrastructure automation, and observability best practices.

Core Capabilities
Intelligent Query Enhancement

User queries are not passed directly to the model. Instead, they are pre-processed and enhanced to improve clarity, completeness, and tool alignment.

Expands vague or underspecified queries into structured intents
Injects relevant context to improve downstream tool execution
Normalizes user input for consistent agent behavior

This significantly reduces ambiguity and improves response accuracy, especially for multi-step workflows like order lookups.

AI Orchestration & Tooling

The system uses a LangGraph-based ReAct agent to dynamically reason about user requests and invoke backend tools via MCP (Model Context Protocol).

Dynamic tool selection based on user intent
Strict tool dependency for all critical data (inventory, orders, pricing)
No hallucinated responses — all outputs must be grounded in tool results
MCP Integration

The agent connects to internal services via a streaming MCP endpoint:

Supports real-time tool execution via SSE
Decouples AI logic from backend systems
Enables scalable, service-oriented architecture


Guardrails & Safety

A multi-layered guardrail system ensures reliability, security, and professional behavior.

Input Guardrails
Detects and blocks prompt injection attempts
Sanitizes malformed or adversarial inputs
Output Guardrails
Prevents leakage of internal prompts or system details
Enforces a consistent, customer-safe tone
Filters restricted or unsafe content
Execution Constraints
Mandatory tool usage for all factual responses
No parameter guessing (e.g., order IDs must come from user or tools)
Timeout protection (60s) to prevent runaway executions

These safeguards ensure the system behaves predictably even under adversarial conditions.

Observability & Monitoring

The platform is designed with production-grade observability to monitor performance, cost, and reliability.

Structured Logging
Centralized logger (Meridian_Support_Engine)
Captures:
Tool connection status
Agent reasoning steps
Execution errors
Performance Metrics
Request-level latency tracking
X-Process-Time header injected into responses
End-to-end timing visibility
Token & Cost Monitoring
Tracks token usage per request/user
Logs metadata for cost analysis and optimization
Health Checks
Root endpoint (/) for instant service health validation
Useful for load balancers and uptime monitoring


Infrastructure & Deployment
Containerization
Fully Dockerized frontend and backend
Cross-platform builds (linux/amd64)
Automated via deploy.sh
Terraform (Infrastructure as Code)

Infrastructure is provisioned using Terraform for reproducibility and scalability:

Amazon ECR for container storage
IAM roles with scoped permissions
AWS App Runner for managed deployment
Environment Configuration

Secure runtime configuration via environment variables:

OPENAI_API_KEY
MCP_SERVER_URL

This setup enables seamless, repeatable deployments across environments.


Testing Strategy

A comprehensive test suite ensures both correctness and resilience.

Agent Tests
Mock MCP/SSE connections
Validate tool loading and reasoning logic
Ensure deterministic agent behavior
API Tests
Verify endpoint responses
Validate error handling for missing configs
Ensure system stability under edge cases

Run tests:

cd backend
pytest tests/ -v
